d J. [R-OH-2]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-04-30","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"OH"},{"bioguideId":"F000470","fullName":"Rep. Fischbach, Michelle [R-MN-7]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-04-30","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"MN"},{"bioguideId":"E000235","fullName":"Rep. Ezell, Mike [R-MS-4]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-05-06","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"MS"},{"bioguideId":"H001100","fullName":"Rep. Hurd, Jeff [R-CO-3]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-05-06","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"CO"},{"bioguideId":"C001118","fullName":"Rep. Cline, Ben [R-VA-6]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-05-06","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"VA"},{"bioguideId":"D000594","fullName":"Rep. De La Cruz, Monica [R-TX-15]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-05-06","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"TX"},{"bioguideId":"M001240","fullName":"Rep. McDowell, Addison P. [R-NC-6]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-05-20","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NC"},{"bioguideId":"H001102","fullName":"Rep. Harris, Mark [R-NC-8]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-05-21","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NC"},{"bioguideId":"R000609","fullName":"Rep. Rutherford, John H. [R-FL-5]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-06-04","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"FL"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T19:33:16+00:00","id":"hr1041-119","introducedDate":"2025-02-06","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2026-06-02","text":"Received in the Senate and Read twice and referred to the Committee on Veterans' Affairs."},"laws":[],"number":"1041","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Armed Forces and National Security","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"B001295","district":12,"fullName":"Rep. Bost, Mike [R-IL-12]","party":"R","state":"IL"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-02-06","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p><strong>Veterans 2nd Amendment Protection Act</strong></p> <p>This bill prohibits the Department of Veterans Affairs (VA) from transmitting certain information to the National Instant Criminal Background Check System (NICS) utilized by licensed importers or dealers of firearms. </p> <p>Specifically, the bill prohibits the VA from transmitting personally identifying information of a veteran or a beneficiary to the NICS solely on the basis that such veteran or beneficiary has an appointed fiduciary to manage their benefits, unless there is an order or finding of a judicial authority that such veteran or beneficiary is a danger to themselves or others.</p>","updateDate":"2025-03-20T20:16:55Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Veterans 2nd Amendment Protection Act","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-08-08T11:19:17Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-08-08T15:18:43Z"}
